    "created_at": "2021-09-24T12:12:32Z",
    "updated_at": "2021-09-24T12:12:32Z",
    "body": "@shimark I could see that concern with the second example, which would likely need to be accompanied by legal regulations to prevent exploitation; but how should this work for the first one? Maybe it wasn't clear enough, but the settings should be completely client-side. It would just be a way not to need to show these cookie banners (browsers automaticaly rejecting not approved cookies), so I don't see how this would be worse than today in the way you mentioned. \r\n\r\nAlso, what do you mean with \"restricting information\"? Stuff like browser versions/settings? Yeah that should probably be done too, but having fundamental \"privacy by design\" (what you mentioned) and then consent/choice on top of that (what I mentioned) is IMO the best way forward (just choice being ineffective regarding privacy, as can be seen in cookie banners)",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
